<title>UK: CRICKET-RAIN STORMS DRENCH LORD'S.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-RAIN STORMS DRENCH LORD'S.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three torrential rain storms drenched Lord's on Sunday delaying a start to the fourth day's play in the second test between England and Australia.</p>
<p>Although the ground was bathed in sunshine in the early afternoon, pools of water lay on the covers and the outfield and there was no immediate prospect of the players taking the field.</p>
<p>Rain washed out Thursday's opening day and only 92 minutes' play were possible on Friday.</p>
<p>Australia, one down in the six-test Ashes series, were 131 for two in reply to England's 77.</p>
</text>
